+# Temple layer: the day as a temple, voice add, rank and streak, weekly review
+
+Plain text for the Help sheet and README (merge by hand). Owner (2026-11-03): "sicker and more useful".
+
+## The Temple (button on Today, palette, All tools; link `#temple`)
+- **Your day as a temple.** A pediment with the date and a sun that follows the clock (a moon at night), the hours as the
+  architrave with a glowing NOW beam, today's events standing between the hour columns. Tap an event to open it.
+- **The steps ahead.** The next 14 days as steps, each as tall as that day's planned work against 60% of its free time:
+  green fits, amber is over the free time, red has a task that may miss its date (a flag on top). **Block time** opens
+  Deadline risk, which puts the task in the best free gap.
+- **Say it.** Tap the mic and say "call Sam tomorrow at 3 pm hashtag nq, high priority". The words are cleaned (word numbers,
+  "p.m.", "at", "hashtag", "every day"), read the way the quick add reads a line, and shown as a chip: **Add** (a time makes
+  it an event) or **Add and listen again**. No service: the phone's own speech recognition. No microphone or no permission:
+  type in the same box. Link `#voice-add`.
+- **Rank and streak.** Your Arena rank, XP and the XP to the next rank, Arena's Daily goal run, and the Planner's own run of
+  days with the daily goal met. Read only (see the notes below).
+- **Weekly review** (link `#weekly-review`). The last 7 days against the 7 before: tasks done, focus minutes, goal days, habit
+  check-ins, done on time, best day, up to 3 laurels (more done than before, goal met on 4+ days, 2h+ focused), and what
+  is dated in the next 7 days. **Copy the week** puts a one-line summary on the clipboard. The Temple button gets a red dot on
+  Saturday to Monday until you open it that day.
+- **Focus mode** gets 60 tick marks that light up as the minutes pass, a comet at the tip of the ring and one line with your
+  rank and streak.
+
+## Notes for the lead (not for the Help sheet)
+- Code: `planner/ext-temple.js`, loaded by one `<script src="ext-temple.js">` in `<head>` after ext-olympus.js. It waits for
+  `planner:ready`, needs `PlannerAPI` (`parseWhen`, `parseTag`, `commit`, `eventsOn`, `freeGaps`, `HB_TOOLS`, `PK_CMDS`) and uses
+  ext-olympus's `window.__ox.line` for the lane layout and ext-flow's `window.__fl.risk` for the flags; without ext-flow the
+  steps simply show no flags.
+- Arena: reads `localStorage['arena.v1']` only (`{ events: [{ id, day, kind }] }`), with Arena's own rules (ranks and XP per
+  kind with the per-day cap, copied from `arena/rules.json`; that file is read once when it is on the same site and replaces the
+  copy if it is valid). A missing or broken ledger = "Arena not opened yet". It never writes any `arena.*` key.
+- Data: none synced. Device key `planner.temple.seen` (the day the review dot was cleared). Tasks and events are added through
+  `snapshot()` + `commit()` exactly like the app's own quick add (Undo works).
+- Effects: follows the Olympus layer (`html.ox`, `html.ox-move`: device switch, `jfx` quality, reduced motion) and its theme
+  variables `--ox-a/--ox-b/--ox-glow`. The only endless animation is the listening pulse (transform / opacity); the Focus ring
+  paints once a second only while Focus mode is open. The Temple adds nothing to the Today page height (one button in the header row).
+- Pure helpers on `window.__tp`: `spoken`, `read`, `arena`, `arenaRules`, `review`, `reviewLine`, `steps`, `run`.
+- Tests: `planner/tests/temple.test.js` (PORT env, default 8789; 42 checks).
